 "goal": {
  "order": 12,
  "title": "12 \u00b7 A line of machines",
  "text": "Items ride tracks a cell a tick. A machine standing just past a track's end takes what the track carries, works on it, and puts what comes out onto the tracks that start beside it. A device whose whole body is one machine word works as that machine.\n\nThe source puts out 16753920, orange. The writer makes it a cube on the track raw; the cutter cuts it into three byte bars, red green blue, onto bars. Put a stacker past the end of bars, where the gap is: it waits for all three bars and stacks them back into the cube, onto whole, and the reader shows its value on seen.",
  "shown": {
   "seen": "16753920"
  },
  "steps": [
   {
    "on": "run",
    "text": "Run it first (F5): the clock starts by itself for a world with tracks. Watch the cube go raw, cut into three bars that queue at the end of bars."
   },
   {
    "on": "sphere",
    "text": "In the palette, graph tab, pick stacker and click the empty cell past the end of bars (x 10). In walk mode the bar holds machines too: pack one with the bar dialog."
   },
   {
    "on": "solved",
    "text": "Press Check to see the stars."
   }
  ]
 },
